## Topic: Battery, sleep and shutting down (src/settings/help_topics.rs)

# Title of the Help topic "Battery, sleep and shutting down".
settings-help-topics-power-title = Battery, sleep and shutting down
# Words people might search for the Help topic "Battery, sleep and shutting down" by, in lower case, separated by spaces.
settings-help-topics-power-keywords = battery power charge sleep suspend shut down turn off restart log out screen
# Help topic "Battery, sleep and shutting down": paragraph 1.
settings-help-topics-power-p1 = Settings, Power shows the battery, the power mode, and how soon, when you are away, the screen dims, locks, turns off and the computer sleeps. Once locking is switched on (see below), Super and L together lock it straight away.
# Help topic "Battery, sleep and shutting down": paragraph 2.
settings-help-topics-power-p2 = Locking is off to begin with. Switch on Lock the screen under Locking on the same page, and choose how long the computer is left alone before it locks: only when it sleeps, or from 1 minute to 2 hours. Your password unlocks it. If you like, add a four-digit PIN as well, which is quicker; choose how long after locking the PIN works, from 15 minutes to 2 hours. After that time, or after five wrong tries, it asks for your password. Locked because it was left alone, the screen shows only the time, drifting about, until you come back; nothing on your screen shows until you are back in. Logging in always needs your password.
# Help topic "Battery, sleep and shutting down": caption and spoken name of picture 3 (settings-power.png).
settings-help-topics-power-pic3 = The Power page
# Help topic "Battery, sleep and shutting down": paragraph 4.
settings-help-topics-power-p4 = When the battery runs down to 10%, a warning appears in the middle of the screen, once, with a sound. Choose another level, or Never, under Warn when the battery is down to. Plugging the charger in or pulling it out shows a card for a few seconds, with a sound, so a lead that slips out is noticed.
# Help topic "Battery, sleep and shutting down": paragraph 5.
settings-help-topics-power-p5 = To log out, restart or shut down, open the ring and click the power button in its middle. The choices cover the middle. Lock and Screensaver happen at once; Suspend, Hibernate, Log out, Restart and Shut down ask twice, filling with the highlight colour and showing a tick at the first click, so a stray click never ends anything. The cross goes back.

